{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways","id":842395,"title":"Why are Open Seal, and various Stealth Gifts NOT Redundant with Step Sideways?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T21:15:58-08:00","id":842395,"title":"Why are Open Seal, and various Stealth Gifts NOT Redundant with Step Sideways?","content":"why is it that anyone bothers learning open seal when step sideways allready makes it possible to ignore a door, or stealth gifts when the umbra llready allows effective invisiblety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T22:50:35-08:00","id":842417,"title":"","content":"Well, Open Seal works on more than doors. You can't &quot;Umbra&quot; into a small safe, or a briefcase, etc.<br /> <br /> Peeking across the Gauntlet is a fairly high difficulty task in urban environments, so stealth boosted with Gifts can easily be better for any sneaky activities in the physical plane. Peeking also leaves you at reduced awareness of your current side of the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> As well... the Umbra is never empty. If you're trying to sneak into a Hive's territory to scout they're numbers and power, the Umbra is going to have patrolling Banes, and BSDs. If you're trying to surveil and lab to monkey wrench it, there are probably Weaver Spiders running around waiting to calcify you. And of course, most creatures with Gnosis can peek the as well.<br /> <br /> Treating the Umbra as a free pass is going to radically change the values of lots of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:57:40-08:00","id":842473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=842417#post842417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treating the Umbra as a free pass is going to radically change the values of lots of powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the potential complications, the time you may need to cross, potential low Gnosis, and the fact that the Umbra on the other side might be completley different and unhelpful, it's a bit silly to consider it as the One True Way :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:49:28-08:00","id":842707,"title":"","content":"To enter and exit the spirit world, you need a reflective surface, a low umbra, high gnosis, some measure of safety on the other side of the Gauntlet, and multiple successes to do it quickly. If you just want to move stealthily, it's much easier to stay in the Realm and use appropriate stealth abilities and powers.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if you are against people who know nothing about the umbra and suck back doors work, then they are probably people you can avoid without going in it. If they are people who know about the umbra, then it's dangerous to assume the back door is actually safe to use.<br /> <br /> In my games, I hold that entering the spirit world is important and players should do it appropriately. Using it as a means of convenience is against its purpose as a storytelling tool. If it makes sense to the players in your game to use it as mere convenience, the ST needs to give some thought as to how he is presenting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T15:26:39-08:00","id":843157,"title":"","content":"One doesn't need a reflective surface in all edition - revised for example doesn't need one and W20 probably has the difficulty raised by one if the mirror isn't stationary but a hand held mirror is enough. Also, if time isn't an issue, the rolls are fairly beatable, and with only the highest gnosis in the pack rolled, the chances of problems while stepping sideways are manageable.<br /> <br /> That said, in the Umbra, even the Penumbra, laws of physics, time and space aren't necessarily as one would know them from the material world. And a place which in essence is a locked place, like a bank vault, would in the umbra be a castle, or similar construct that conveys that essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:36:02-08:00","id":845416,"title":"","content":"ok similar question, is it still reasonable for a Garou with Open Seal to get training and equipment for conventional lock picking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:52:07-08:00","id":845427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=845416#post845416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok similar question, is it still reasonable for a Garou with Open Seal to get training and equipment for conventional lock picking...</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh yeah....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:24:06-08:00","id":845440,"title":"","content":"To the OP: Something that just &quot;unlocks&quot; or &quot;wasn't locked&quot; doesn't break the veil. You can use it in public and (in most cases) it's going to seem like pure luck, or a coincidence that the door you tried to get into just didn't seem to latch, or whatnot.<br /> <br /> To the second question about lock-picking... Gnosis can be a resource best used elsewhere. Sometimes picking that lock might take a few more seconds, but using that extra point of Gnosis might just get you through the Gauntlet, help you activate a Gift, feed a Spirit for a favor, or have other uses not too far into the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T01:00:57-08:00","id":845513,"title":"","content":"It pretty much never hurts to have mundane training instead of relying on just Gifts. It doesn't hurt that a lot of Gifts will use the relevant Attributes and Abilities that represent that training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T06:33:58-08:00","id":845595,"title":"","content":"Has 'Open Seal' gnosis cost in W20 - for I don't think that the gift had. Only reason to still carry lock picking tools is so you can enter a place with high gauntlet areas (but such places might also have high security lock, or need iris scans and what not). Also, lock pick set needs to be dedicated, so it requires a permanent gnosis otherwise free for dedicating other stuff.<br /> <br /> So, I wouldn't use a lock pick set, but invest experience into Gnosis (always a good choice, although low level ragabash have few gifts that need spending gnosis).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:53:32-08:00","id":846095,"title":"","content":"oh curious just thought? Would open seal work on a car?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:59:21-08:00","id":846101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846095#post846095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious just thought? Would open seal work on a car?</div> </div> </div> </div>To open the door or trunk yes, start the car no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:25:13-08:00","id":846128,"title":"","content":"which gift do I want to start the car then?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:27:42-08:00","id":846131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846128#post846128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which gift do I want to start the car then?</div> </div> </div> </div>What gifts control technology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:46:40-08:00","id":846150,"title":"","content":"Actually, I don't see why Open Seal wouldn't let you override the lock on the starter. It wouldn't start the car, but it would let you turn the ignition switch without a key (though you'd probably need something like a screwdriver to engage it).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:53:49-08:00","id":846157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846150#post846150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't see why Open Seal wouldn't let you override the lock on the starter. It wouldn't start the car, but it would let you turn the ignition switch without a key (though you'd probably need something like a screwdriver to engage it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on a modern car, though. That won't fly without Control Complex Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:54:03-08:00","id":846158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846150#post846150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't see why Open Seal wouldn't let you override the lock on the starter. It wouldn't start the car, but it would let you turn the ignition switch without a key (though you'd probably need something like a screwdriver to engage it).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all modern cars have a chip in the key as an anti theft feature, without it the engine won't function properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T14:25:46-08:00","id":846271,"title":"","content":"Even with all that cars out there without it (of which there are plenty), and the ones that someone's bypassed (since a lot of people do that once their car is 5+ years old because it's cheaper to bypass it for ~$25 bucks than the hassle of a $200+ new chipped key, and depreciation on the car has made investing in security less of a priority), there's a lot of interpretation wiggle room here.<br /> <br /> Nothing in Open Seal says it doesn't work if there's an electronic aspect of the lock. I can see the argument to say you'd need to use Open Seal every time with such a device (since it &quot;reseals&quot; automatically in away a purely physical lock doesn't), but not letting Open Seal work on anything with this sort of countermeasure is getting close to making it useless in modern-day games.<br /> <br /> Lots of business and schools have a similar feature on their doors. The door has a physical lock, and you need a card/fob/etc. to disengage it. Are all of these doors now impenetrable to Open Seal? If not... what's the difference?<br /> <br /> If a safe has a fingerprint scanner on top of a combination lock... is Open Seal likewise off the table? Again, if not, what's the difference?<br /> <br /> Also, with the whole &quot;what's the difference&quot; thing, it's a Gift, not physics. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T15:57:48-08:00","id":846311,"title":"","content":"The difference is in the ignition. Modern cars have the whole system done as a single joint electronic system that ties user identification, ignition, reporting to the owner and checking core functions. The concept of Open Seal is opening locks, not controlling complex systems.<br /> <br /> Would you allow Open Seal to work against encrypted files or password locked machines? I've always seen it as quite literal opening - as in there is something mechanically locked at some point, so you make that thing released. You do not affect electronics, you just get whatever is keeping the container/doorway closed to move.<br /> <br /> The idea of locks is that they are what stops the mechanical stuff holding the thing closed from opening. Open Seal just skips the internals and allows you to get to the other side. It doesn't allow you to control the system or understand the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:43:32-08:00","id":846459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846311#post846311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is in the ignition. Modern cars have the whole system done as a single joint electronic system that ties user identification, ignition, reporting to the owner and checking core functions. The concept of Open Seal is opening locks, not controlling complex systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't answer any of the other examples I brought up.<br /> <br /> As well, Open Seal is opening a lock (the lock that's stopping you from activating the starter motor switch). You're not controlling a complex system, you're skipping the internals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you allow Open Seal to work against encrypted files or password locked machines? </div> </div> </div>Encrypted files are out solely on the wording of the power. It only works on physical devices. A file isn't a physical device.<br /> <br /> A password lock would need more detail. A keypad on an automatic door is a &quot;password locked machine&quot; that would count because you're working on the physical device of the door. Logging into a password locked computer wouldn't work because the lock is digital on digital software; the physical device of the computer is effectively open to you already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've always seen it as quite literal opening - as in there is something mechanically locked at some point, so you make that thing released. You do not affect electronics, you just get whatever is keeping the container/doorway closed to move. </div> </div> </div>This seems too literal for a magical power. If you can't affect electronics, a huge number of common place locks are immune because they have electronic components essential to engaging the mechanism. <br /> <br /> So, if Open Seal can unlock a door by circumventing the electronics controlling the mechanism and just move the latch, why can't Open Seal unlock an ignition by circumventing the electronics and allowing the physical switch to engage to complete the starter circuit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea of locks is that they are what stops the mechanical stuff holding the thing closed from opening. Open Seal just skips the internals and allows you to get to the other side. It doesn't allow you to control the system or understand the system. </div> </div> </div>Neither is relevant here though. You're not controlling a system, you're skipping a lock on a switch. The Gift isn't granting understanding either..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:01:44-08:00","id":846465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846459#post846459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, Open Seal is opening a lock (the lock that's stopping you from activating the starter motor switch). You're not controlling a complex system, you're skipping the internals.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This bypass your talking about is essentially hotwiring the car or blocking out an aspect of the anti-theft system. In most cases if the chip isn\u2019t detected the cylinder won\u2019t even unlock (Haha double lock!) but lets say for grins you open seal both locks and get the cylinder to turn.....<br /> <br /> Congratulations you have gotten the motor to turn over, now with out the signal from the chip not only will the alarm sound but you could <br /> A: Cause the injectors to not toggle<br /> B: Kill the fuel pump (good luck going more then 15 feet)<br /> C: Cause the spark plugs not to fire.<br /> <br /> All cars sold in the major nations of Europe have required an immoblizer system sine the late 90's, The big four had cars with them from the early 90's some going back to the late 80's. <br /> <br /> Sounds like a complex system to me.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T01:15:09-08:00","id":846495,"title":"","content":"Ok, so we can just head this off then:<br /> <br /> 1) Open Seal can effectively hotwire a car by letting you turn the ignition via bypassing the locks on it (electronic or not).<br /> 2) Open Seal isn't going to deactivate any other security measures the car happens to have; which I never argued it would, just like it wouldn't disarm plenty of alarm systems on doors or windows because they activate regardless of whether or not you opened the locks on them with the right key.<br /> <br /> Seems settled to me. The point was, &quot;start the car,&quot; not, &quot;operate the car for an extended period of time with no other complications.&quot; How effective Open Seal is for this is going to be exceedingly dependent on where you are, and lots of factors about the car itself.<br /> <br /> As I said up thread, Gifts aren't a good replacement for training and mundane tools. They might do in a pinch, but if you're going to be stealing cars a lot, learn how to do it without Gifts; esp. since this will cover things like learning which cars are good targets if you need to fall back on Gifts because you're in a rush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T03:32:34-07:00","id":846504,"title":"","content":"Open Seal opens or unlocks a physical device. If the car's ignition has a steering wheel lock on it, Open Seal will unlock that. It won't activate the car or even turn the ignition far enough to engage the starter motor. That could be achieved by Control Simple Machine, but as noted that would just turn the ignition and engage the starter, it wouldn't disengage any complex disabling technology. Control Complex Machine would allow the Garou to run the entire car without the keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:25:08-07:00","id":846533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846495#post846495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so we can just head this off then:<br /> <br /> 1) Open Seal can effectively hotwire a car by letting you turn the ignition via bypassing the locks on it (electronic or not).<br /> 2) Open Seal isn't going to deactivate any other security measures the car happens to have; which I never argued it would, just like it wouldn't disarm plenty of alarm systems on doors or windows because they activate regardless of whether or not you opened the locks on them with the right key.<br /> <br /> Seems settled to me. The point was, &quot;start the car,&quot; not, &quot;operate the car for an extended period of time with no other complications.&quot; How effective Open Seal is for this is going to be exceedingly dependent on where you are, and lots of factors about the car itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the point. Traditional car locks work in such a way that you need to insert the appropriate key and then turn it to start ignition. I would completley agree with you that if you put in a screwdriver or a nailfile or something and then use open seal that you could ignite the traditional car.<br /> <br /> The &quot;unlocking&quot; has nothing to do with a modern car. The electronics that start the car are not &quot;locked&quot;, ignition itself is not directly tied to the turning of the key. The lock is less of a open something and more of a i have to add a whole piece of the electrical system for the car to be able to operate. It's like claiming that open seal would allow the car to work if I pulled out the sparkplugs.<br /> <br /> Besides, open Seal is a oneshot thing. It's not an ongoing effect. The modern car dies immediatley if the key is no longer present, and even if you do manage to turn it, within 3 seconds Open Seal wouldn't be working any more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:28:17-07:00","id":846534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846504#post846504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open Seal opens or unlocks a physical device. If the car's ignition has a steering wheel lock on it, Open Seal will unlock that. It won't activate the car or even turn the ignition far enough to engage the starter motor. That could be achieved by Control Simple Machine, but as noted that would just turn the ignition and engage the starter, it wouldn't disengage any complex disabling technology. Control Complex Machine would allow the Garou to run the entire car without the keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool, semi-official anwser! Isn't a ignition system a bit too complex for Control Simple Machine, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T06:02:17-07:00","id":846544,"title":"","content":"Oh similar question on Speach of the world, it has no activation cost, only reason I can see to learn a language once you have it is... if your wanting to reflect growing close to a culture... like a native american tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:33:00-07:00","id":846627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846544#post846544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh similar question on Speach of the world, it has no activation cost, only reason I can see to learn a language once you have it is... if your wanting to reflect growing close to a culture... like a native american tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you ever think &quot;this is a valid question to ask? Or &quot; maybe I'm just not reading this right&quot; before you click post reply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:13:35-07:00","id":846696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846627#post846627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you ever think &quot;this is a valid question to ask? Or &quot; maybe I'm just not reading this right&quot; before you click post reply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was asking &quot;Am I missing something, there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:47:39-07:00","id":846713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846533#post846533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;unlocking&quot; has nothing to do with a modern car. The electronics that start the car are not &quot;locked&quot;, ignition itself is not directly tied to the turning of the key.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is mostly settled, my problem is this assertion that &quot;modern&quot; is some important distinction here. Immobilizers have existed in various forms for almost 100 years. While the current common immobilizers have become standard (even regulated as such) in lots of places, they're not universal. Unless your sole definition of &quot;modern car,&quot; is, &quot;got rid of steering wheel ignition keys, and has a transponder based immobilizer,&quot; it's inaccurate. Not every market has this as a legal requirement. Japan, for example, has been making cars without this specific technology to this day. Most of their companies still consider it a luxury thing/thing for exports to places that have it as law (and I can speak to this with personal experience considering my current car is a Japanese make, well after most developed countries made these things a requirement, and it doesn't have one). Has Honda or Toyota not made a modern car in 15+ years because they consider this an optional bit of technology; all the other new technologies be damned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T17:17:33-07:00","id":846810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=846534#post846534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh cool, semi-official anwser! Isn't a ignition system a bit too complex for Control Simple Machine, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly a YMMV point - the way I'm interpreting it, you're not controlling the ignition system. All you're doing is causing a cylinder to roll. That's the simply machine you have control over. Everything else is a consequence of that cylinder rolling, but you have no control over it. If the battery fails, or some other fault occurs, that's beyond the scope of controlling the simple machine.<br /> <br /> Look at it this way - you could also cause a lever to flip, and whatever else happens due to that lever flipping (like it being the emergency kill switch of a hydro-electric dam) is entirely beyond the scope of the Gift.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:33:17-07:00","id":915293,"title":"","content":"oh a somewhat similar question how effective is Taking the forgotten?<br /> <br /> it doesnt help with the actual theft, just with causing the victim to forget he ever owned it<br /> <br /> If I Use it in a store after I nick something, does the store forget an item belonged to them? Or what, trying to find a way to make the gift worthwhile to a garou thief, or agent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T22:05:08-07:00","id":915404,"title":"","content":"The Gift, as written, works on individuals, not institutions or systems. The store clerk wouldn't remember the object being the store (though if it is something they have multiples of it wouldn't erase the fact that they carry the item), but it wouldn't remove the item from the inventory software.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T05:11:46-07:00","id":915523,"title":"","content":"ok, any ideas on gifts that are good for larcenous garou of any stripe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:46:02-07:00","id":915565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways?p=915523#post915523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, any ideas on gifts that are good for larcenous garou of any stripe?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the ones mentioned in the thread so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T10:21:39-07:00","id":915692,"title":"","content":"The Ragabash, Homid, Glasswalker,and Bone Gnawer lists are full of decent options (this shouldn't really be surprising) though there's decent options via the social oriented lists (Philodox - though very out of Auspice to use those Gifts that way - and Galliard), or less direct guile stuff (Children of Gaia and Fianna). Basically too much to just list (and then all the Changeling Breeds like Bastet and Nuwisha that have some nice ones as well).<br /> <br /> Basically, there's enough options that &quot;any stripe&quot; makes it too hard to narrow down a list. Once you get down to things like, &quot;Con Artist,&quot; &quot;High Tech Security Cracker,&quot; etc, it's a lot easier to form a smaller list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T10:22:56-07:00","id":915694,"title":"","content":"pick pocket?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:01:32-07:00","id":915749,"title":"","content":"In case it might help go a bit faster... Rank limits? Like just 1-2, or the whole lists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:05:02-07:00","id":915786,"title":"","content":"whole list, im mostly thinking in the early rank stage, but even elder bone gnawers probaly pick pockets to get by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T18:59:23-07:00","id":915965,"title":"","content":"Ok, so this probably isn't a complete list, but screw it, it's long enough. I'm not repeating Gifts that appear in multiple lists. I left out a few things that could be arguable because they're too obvious in my mind. Comments are what they are, I think it's pretty self explanatory.<br /> <br /> Homid -<br /> 1:<br /> Apecraft's Blessing (if you use any tools in your pick-pocketing for distractions or hiding things)<br /> Persuasion (In case of suspicion after a bump)<br /> Smell of Man (Pets are a good in on a mark)<br /> 2:<br /> Divide (good distraction Gift)<br /> Jam Technology (another good distraction, as well as getting rid of cameras)<br /> Mark of the Wolf (another back-up Gift since it will make your mark less likely to be believed by authorities if they realize what happened)<br /> Speech of the World (only if travelling or in a diverse city and you don't invest in languages)<br /> 3:<br /> Tongues (Same reasons as Speech of the World, also good for deciphering gang tags and avoiding trouble from that)<br /> 4:<br /> Body Shift (If for some reason you haven't maxed out Dexterity)<br /> Bury the Wolf (Draw less attention to yourself by removing the effects of the Curse)<br /> 5:<br /> Assimilation (See Speech of the World/Tongues)<br /> Beyond Human (even better than Bury the Wolf for approaching and manipulating a mark while you rob them)<br /> <br /> Metis -<br /> 2:<br /> Form Mastery (makes it easier to do partial shifts which can be all sorts of useful)<br /> 3:<br /> Chameleon (stealth)<br /> 5:<br /> Madness (distractions)<br /> Totem Gift (distractions again)<br /> <br /> Lupus -<br /> 1:<br /> Heightened Senses (easier time finding good marks)<br /> 5:<br /> Boon of the Animal Fathers (note this is an old Gift, might not be allowed, but you can get some of the nice bonuses for Cunning Totem animals without having to have them as your Totem)<br /> <br /> Ragabash -<br /> 1:<br /> Blur of the Milky Eye (Stealth)<br /> Hush (Back up)<br /> Infectious Laughter (Back-up if you get caught, crack a joke and they laugh so hard they forget if you're careful)<br /> Liar's Face (Approach the mark/back up)<br /> Open Seal (in case you steal something locked)<br /> 2:<br /> Blissful Ignorance (situational stealth)<br /> Emergency Exit (back up)<br /> Obscure the Truth (Super lying)<br /> Pulse of the Prey (if you're after something specific)<br /> Spider's Song (finding a good mark)<br /> Taking the Forgotten (pretty much the pick-pocket Gift)<br /> Trickster Beacon (Distraction)<br /> 3:<br /> Gremlins (distractions and mucking with any on-person security like proximity sensors)<br /> Impunity (back up)<br /> Liar's Craft (super lying)<br /> Riddle (distraction)<br /> The Usual Suspects (if you want to track multiple repeat marks)<br /> 4:<br /> Madness Season (distraction)<br /> 5:<br /> Blank (Everyone else holds still for a short period of time and ignores everything unless attacked)<br /> Thousand Forms (shift into animals that people ignore and are dexterous)<br /> <br /> Theurge -<br /> 3:<br /> Pulse of the Invisible (watch people from the Umbra more easily)<br /> 4:<br /> Grasp the Beyond (take things across the Gauntlet without having to dedicate them first)<br /> Shadowplay (distractions, or even stealing things with the shadow)<br /> <br /> Philodox -<br /> 2:<br /> King of Beats (get animals to do stuff for you)<br /> 4:<br /> Roll Over (mugging without violence)<br /> <br /> Galliard -<br /> 1:<br /> Beast Speech (talk to the animals)<br /> 2:<br /> Distractions<br /> Dreamspeak (gather intel)<br /> Reverie (distraction, maybe snag information as well)<br /> 3:<br /> Song of Rage (distraction, back up to get the mark in trouble)<br /> 5:<br /> Headgames (distractions and mark approach)<br /> <br /> Ahroun -<br /> 1:<br /> Falling Touch (knock the mark over &quot;accidentally&quot;)<br /> 2:<br /> Spirit of the Fray (Always be faster than your mark)<br /> True Fear (distraction)<br /> 4:<br /> Touch of Rage (distraction)<br /> <br /> Black Furies -<br /> 1:<br /> Owl's Speech (if owls are around)<br /> Spirit Smugler (Camp Gift, shove small things into the Umbra)<br /> 2:<br /> Curse of Aeolus (stealth and distraction)<br /> Kneel (distraction)<br /> 4:<br /> Body Wrack (distraction)<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers -<br /> 1:<br /> Smell of Success (find good marks)<br /> Smell of Sweet Honey (distraction, easier to track the mark as they try to get away from the pests)<br /> 2:<br /> Find the Prize (find what you're looking to steal)<br /> Guise of the Hound (stealth, since dog)<br /> 3:<br /> Beg<br /> Call the Rust (distraction, back up)<br /> Gift of the Termite (distraction)<br /> 4:<br /> Attunement (intel gathering)<br /> Blink (back up)<br /> Face in the Crowd (distraction)<br /> Infest (distraction)<br /> Trust Me (super lying)<br /> 5:<br /> Gluttony (old Gift, hide almost anything in your stomach for later)<br /> Help Me<br /> Riot<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia<br /> 1:<br /> Brother's Scent (blend in)<br /> 3:<br /> Chant of Morpheus (put people to sleep)<br /> Dazzle (distraction)<br /> Guilt Trip<br /> 5:<br /> Trust of Gaia<br /> <br /> Fianna -<br /> 1:<br /> Fairie Light (distraction)<br /> 2:<br /> Brew (get people drunk without them realizing it)<br /> Glib Tongue (super lying)<br /> Fair Fortune (reroll a bad roll, good for everything really)<br /> 4:<br /> Faerie Blood (old Gift, most for the Gnosis saving since a lot of these Gifts cost Gnosis)<br /> Phantasm (distraction)<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris -<br /> 3:<br /> Loki's Touch (distraction)<br /> Mark the Enemy (tag a mark for later)<br /> 5:<br /> Strength of the Ancestors (boost any Attributes so Dex/Socials/Wits, requires high Ancestors Background to be worth it)<br /> <br /> Glasswalkers -<br /> <br /> 1:<br /> Control Simple Machine<br /> Plug and Play (Your smartphone lets you steal all sorts of digital stuff)<br /> Skyscrapper Vision (gather intel, follow marks from range)<br /> Weaver's Eyes (Pick pocket encrypted transmissions!)<br /> 2:<br /> Cybersenses (gather intel, track mark)<br /> Heat Metal (distraction)<br /> Image of the Saints (Camp Gift, helps pick good marks)<br /> Mind Partition (Camp Gift, lets you set up complicated picks quickly)<br /> Pennies from Heaven (back up)<br /> 3:<br /> Control Complex Machine<br /> Intrusion (back up for a pick pocket unless the mark is in a hard to get to place)<br /> 4:<br /> Doppelganger (stealth, approach mark, back up)<br /> Tractor Beam (pull stuff into the Umbra)<br /> 5:<br /> Calm the Flock (ignore the Curse)<br /> Chaos Mechanics (always useful)<br /> Phone Travel (back up, get into hard to reach places)<br /> Song of the City-Beast (distraction)<br /> <br /> Red Talons -<br /> 1:<br /> Cub's Lesson (Camp Gift, crappy back up... but Red Talon theif?)<br /> Wolf at the Door (control the mark's location)<br /> 2:<br /> Primal Instinct (distraction with enough successes, setup a mark with less)<br /> 5:<br /> Blessing of the First Pack (Ragabash option only)<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords -<br /> 1:<br /> Dreams of a Thousand Cranes (Hakken Gift, always useful)<br /> Fair Path (Hakken Gift, social boost)<br /> Seizing the Edge (back up)<br /> Shadow Weaving (distraction, stealh)<br /> Whisper Catching (intel gathering)<br /> 2:<br /> Hidding Secret (Camp Gift, intel gathering, explicitly blackmail the Gift)<br /> 3:<br /> Curse of Corruption (back up, good for discrediting others)<br /> Dark of Night (Hakken Gift, blinds the target)<br /> 4:<br /> Seeds of Doubt (super lying)<br /> Ubiquitous Presence (keep the mark completely off their game)<br /> 5:<br /> Obedience (Mind control)<br /> <br /> Silent Striders -<br /> 1:<br /> Silence (stealth)<br /> 4:<br /> Touch of Death (Camp Gift, a bit overboard for pickpocketing, but subtly renders the target catatonic and forgets how things happened)<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs -<br /> 1:<br /> Eye of the Falcon (not as good as Heightened Senses for pick pockets, but similar)<br /> New Moon's Laughter (Lodge Gift, setup marks)<br /> 5:<br /> New Moon Legerdemain (Lodge Gift, pack of trickster spirits for your personal use)<br /> <br /> Stargazers -<br /> 3:<br /> Conundrum (distraction)<br /> <br /> Uktena -<br /> 1:<br /> Moonstruck Path (track the mark if you lose them and it's dark outside)<br /> Shroud (stealth, distraction)<br /> 2:<br /> Overlook (stealth)<br /> Reveal the Hidden (good if you know what you're looking for)<br /> Shadows at Dawn (back up, tell the mark true stuff about you and they'll forgot it later)<br /> Sight of Hidden Places (could theoretically see hidden pockets and such)<br /> 3:<br /> Invisibility<br /> Scrying (intel gathering, track the mark at range)<br /> Secrets (intel gathering)<br /> 4:<br /> Bare the Heart (intel gathering)<br /> <br /> Wendigo -<br /> 2:<br /> Fog (stealth, distraction)<br /> Speak with Wind Spirits (intel gathering, maybe finding a mark if you lose them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https